(characters)
  > (character)
    (name) Corrigan
    (role) Private Investigator
    (book) Volume I: The Streets of Thornus
    (description) A cynical detective who hunted his own shadow and found it. After the incident at the St. Marlowe, he is said to walk without a reflection—a hollow vessel haunting the streets of Predymesh.
    (status) Alive (Hollow / Shadowless)

  > (character)
    (name) Doctor Blade
    (role) Physician & Assassin
    (book) Volume III: The RedLink Arc
    (description) A legendary healer with a dark secret. He cures the incurable and kills with the same precision using the magical Alilberry.
    (status) Alive

  > (character)
    (name) Master Vorn
    (role) Merchant
    (book) Volume III: The RedLink Arc
    (description) A wealthy merchant, cheat, and slaver who sought a cure for his gout and found eternal rest instead.
    (status) Deceased

  > (character)
    (name) Sultan of Butterflies
    (role) Comedian / Cult Leader
    (book) Volume IV: The Resistance
    (description) A tall, beautiful, and sharp-witted widow turned comedian. She hides her quest for justice behind a mask of madness and punchlines. She spent her husband's last relic—the Viyu cufflink—to scream the truth through the RedLink.
    (status) Alive (Active)

  > (character)
    (name) Galarian "Galar" Freiton
    (role) Scientist
    (book) Volume IV: The Resistance
    (description) A brilliant scientist who spent 13 years discovering the "Soul of Viyu", a dark free energy source. Killed eleven years ago to keep it secret.
    (status) Deceased

  > (character)
    (name) Agent Sprite
    (role) Government Agent
    (book) Volume IV: The Resistance
    (description) A shadowy government operative involved in the assassination of Galarian Freiton.
    (status) Alive

  > (character)
    (name) Agent Laozi
    (role) Government Agent
    (book) Volume IV: The Resistance
    (description) A shadowy government operative involved in the assassination of Galarian Freiton.
    (status) Alive

  > (character)
    (name) Aester Cloudwear
    (role) Real Estate Developer
    (book) Volume II: The Cost of Sin
    (description) A wealthy tycoon who manipulated the War of Fourbournes to gentrify Glareach. A monster in a silk suit who built a sin city on the bones of the poor. He bought the contract on the Sultan's life through three shell companies and a poker table at the St. Marlowe.
    (status) Alive (Wealthy)

  > (character)
    (name) Lorhud Krauper
    (role) Hitman / Former Soldier
    (book) Volume II: The Cost of Sin
    (description) A drug-addicted veteran seeking revenge for his daughter Lenia. He wears a green beret with 22 stars and walked the razor's edge between healing and death, until the night in the alley behind The Laughing Stock when he refused the contract on the Sultan and took her hand instead—trading the berry for the memory.
    (status) Alive (Remembering)

  > (character)
    (name) Lenia Krauper
    (role) Seamstress / Victim
    (book) Volume II: The Cost of Sin
    (description) Lorhud's beloved daughter. During the razing of Glareach, she was dragged from her home by Cloudwear's private security. She was violated and butchered by Aester himself as her father watched helplessly from the shadows, her blood serving as the mortar for the first casino of the new Glareach.
    (status) Deceased

  > (character)
    (name) Klaude Barral
    (role) Chronomancer / Horologist
    (book) Volume II: The Cost of Sin
    (description) A master clockmaker who uses ash from destroyed cities to power his Chronometers. He allows people to relive their past, but he never lets them change it. Since the eleven-hour pulse began killing his instruments, he moves den to den through the ruins of old Glareach.
    (status) Alive (Cynical)

  > (character)
    (name) Dr. Brann Corshield
    (role) Chief Alienist / Villain
    (book) Volume III: The RedLink Arc
    (description) An immensely egotistical psychiatrist who ran St. Jude's Asylum. Obsessed with his own image (literally) and maintaining "order," he sought to lobotomize the Sultan of Butterflies to silence her "delusions," and built the RedLink in the asylum's restricted wing.
    (status) Unknown (Lost in the Fall of St. Jude's)

  > (character)
    (name) Valeth Vanceshire
    (role) Diplomat
    (book) Volume I: The Streets of Thornus
    (description) A kind-hearted foreign diplomat visiting Thornus. Armed only with his navy blue notebook, he documents the corruption of the ruling class while trying to navigate a dangerous political landscape.
    (status) Alive (Observant)

  > (character)
    (name) Wulf Kosnak
    (role) Shadow Ruler / Corrupt Noble
    (book) Volume I: The Streets of Thornus
    (description) A grotesque, gluttonous veteran who pulls the strings of Thornus from behind the curtain. He displays the skulls of his wife's parents as trophies, a secret he keeps from her.
    (status) Alive (Corrupt)

  > (character)
    (name) Penta Kosnak
    (role) Noblewoman / Prisoner
    (book) Volume I: The Streets of Thornus
    (description) The young, beautiful, and intelligent wife of Wulf Kosnak. A spoil of war forced into marriage, she is a prisoner in her own home, unaware of the gruesome truth hanging above her head.
    (status) Alive (Trapped)

  > (character)
    (name) Ophera
    (role) Sewer Dweller / Listener
    (book) Volume I: The Streets of Thornus
    (description) The eldest of the sewer-dwelling triplets. She "listens" to the vibrations of the city through the iron pipes, gathering secrets that wash down from above.
    (status) Alive (Hidden)

  > (character)
    (name) Melsani
    (role) Sewer Dweller / Watcher
    (book) Volume I: The Streets of Thornus
    (description) One of the triplets. She watches the reflections in the city's grime and puddles, seeing truths that people try to hide in the light.
    (status) Alive (Hidden)

  > (character)
    (name) Nopilai
    (role) Sewer Dweller / Scenter
    (book) Volume I: The Streets of Thornus
    (description) The brother of the triplets. He can smell fear, blood, and corruption in the steam that rises from the grates of Predymesh.
    (status) Alive (Hidden)

  > (character)
    (name) Pellera Orlong
    (role) Daughter / Patient Zero
    (book) Volume III: The RedLink Arc
    (description) Afflicted at nine, the first human to manifest the 'Touch of Rose'. Now twelve, she remains in a vegetative state in a slum attic, her forehead marked by a crimson rose-leaf shape. She is the biological 'Zero Point' for the disease, and her mark is a beacon for a connection that hasn't been established yet.
    (status) Ailing (Vegetative)

  > (character)
    (name) Nex Orlong
    (role) Mason turned Thief
    (book) Volume III: The RedLink Arc
    (description) Once an honest mason, Nex turned to a life of crime to fund the Alilberry treatment needed to save his daughter. He is desperate, guilt-ridden, and now in possession of dangerous secrets.
    (status) Alive (Wanted)

  > (character)
    (name) Avalia Krones
    (role) Scientist / Strategist
    (book) Volume IV: The Resistance
    (description) A brilliant strategist who secretly used Proxanian Seeds and Sansu Syrup to develop her formula. She sought to create a botanical neural network but never intended to create a pathogen. After demanding to see Patient Zero (Pellera Orlong), she realized Willare's mistake involved her secret Proxanian materials. She remains silent about the source to protect her own life and research.
    (status) Alive (Strategically Silent)

  > (character)
    (name) Willare Frindjen
    (role) Junior Lab Assistant
    (book) Volume IV: The Resistance
    (description) A dedicated assistant who is consumed by guilt. She accidentally contaminated the Krones Formula with what she thought was a standard supplement (the Crimson Binder). It was only after Avalia forced her to look at Pellera Orlong that she realized the magnitude of her error, though she still doesn't know the Proxanian nature of what she touched.
    (status) Alive (Guilt-Ridden / Broken)

  > (character)
    (name) Proythom
    (role) Farmer / Civilian
    (book) Volume IV: The Resistance
    (description) Willare's former lover. A kind and honest man from the outskirts of Predymesh. Willare left him without explanation to protect him from the guilt and the 'rot' she believed she was carrying.
    (status) Alive (Heartbroken)

  > (character)
    (name) The Mute Bard
    (role) Alchemist's Companion
    (book) Volume III: The RedLink Arc
    (description) A mysterious figure who cannot speak but whose songs hold the power to stabilize volatile herbal mixtures. He provides the final, magical resonance required to turn raw Alilberry into the legendary 'Drop'.
    (status) Unknown

  > (character)
    (name) Prostex Leatherwave
    (role) Caretaker of Cats
    (book) Volume IV: The Resistance
    (description) A young boy in Craninal who lives a simple, peaceful life caring for his three cats in a hidden garden.
    (status) Alive (Happy)

  > (character)
    (name) Soot, Ginger, and Moonbeam
    (role) The Council of Three (Cats)
    (book) Volume IV: The Resistance
    (description) Prostex's three feline companions. Soot is the shadow, Ginger is the sleeper, and Moonbeam is the guardian. They provide the only true peace in the city of Craninal.
    (status) Alive (Purring)

  > (character)
    (name) Rainhold Fredsound
    (role) CEO of Fredsound Dream Studios
    (book) Volume II: The Cost of Sin
    (description) A kind and generous man living in Hamitonis. He manages his massive wealth with a heavy heart, preferring to help others in secret. He loves Kramen as his closest friend.
    (status) Wounded

  > (character)
    (name) Kramen Mandora
    (role) Butler / Guardian
    (book) Volume II: The Cost of Sin
    (description) A strict but loyal butler who grew up in old Glareach before its destruction. He is a skilled marksman and saved Isabylle Fredsound's life during an "accident".
    (status) Active (Wounded)

  > (character)
    (name) Isabylle Fredsound
    (role) Matriarch
    (book) Volume II: The Cost of Sin
    (description) Rainhold's mother, who refused Aester Cloudwear's gentrification project. She was saved by Kramen after a car "accident".
    (status) Alive

  > (character)
    (name) Elyka
    (role) Movie Star
    (book) Volume II: The Cost of Sin
    (description) A glamorous celebrity unimpressed by wealth and fame. She vanished during an ambush in Hamitonis.
    (status) Missing

  > (character)
    (name) Children of the Mountain
    (role) Extinct Civilization (Proxanians)
    (book) Volume III: The RedLink Arc
    (description) A humanoid race that predates human colonization of Thornus. Their culture revolved around the 'Communion Rites' and the biological harvesting of Sansu Syrup. Their remnant psychic frequency, the 'Proxanian Echo', was harvested to power the RedLink.
    (status) Extinct (Harvested)

  > (character)
    (name) Niva DeRosa
    (role) Intelligence Officer
    (book) Volume I: The Streets of Thornus
    (description) A sewer worker's daughter who became an intelligence officer to give her father a better life. She uncovered the plot behind the Massacre of the Grenadiers but was ignored, leading to a tragedy that broke her. She was never seen again under her own name—but someone meticulous now keeps the lights burning in a dead man's office in Predymesh.
    (status) Missing (Presumed Operating as 'Corrigan')

  > (character)
    (name) Donlane DeRosa
    (role) Sewer Worker / "The King"
    (book) Volume I: The Streets of Thornus
    (description) A giant of a man with a crown-shaped birthmark on his hand. He dedicated his life to the sewers of Thornus to raise his children. He died buying flowers in the City Market.
    (status) Deceased

  > (character)
    (name) Granold Rolnifeld
    (role) Major / Military Officer
    (book) Volume I: The Streets of Thornus
    (description) A charismatic but arrogant military officer who dismissed Niva's warning about the City Market attack. He carries the weight of the massacre and Niva's disappearance. He gave his blood and a day of his future to the Chronometer, and came back with burned palms and the truth.
    (status) Alive (Guilt-Ridden)

  > (character)
    (name) Hewond Lynnia
    (role) Mayor
    (book) Volume I: The Streets of Thornus
    (description) The Mayor of Predymesh who was assassinated during the Massacre of the Grenadiers, after asking too many questions about the money that vanished uphill into St. Jude's.
    (status) Deceased

  > (character)
    (name) Soren Perborn
    (role) Retired Fisherman / Former Agent
    (book) Volume V: The Black Ragnarok
    (description) A former operative of Black Ragnarok who retired to a life of fishing in Oakhaven. He was pulled back into the shadows by a cryptic message from his old partner. He carried Freya out of the burning asylum and, for the first time in thirty years, did not look back at the sea.
    (status) Active (Reluctant)

  > (character)
    (name) Freya Haelmar
    (role) Operative
    (book) Volume V: The Black Ragnarok
    (description) An operative of Black Ragnarok and Soren's former partner. After discovering the betrayal within the organization, she infiltrated the RedLink program voluntarily; when Corshield expanded the ward past his first twelve, she made sure she was among the new subjects. She spent two years wired in as Bed Fourteen before Soren carried her out of the burning asylum.
    (status) Recovering (Rescued)

  > (character)
    (name) Vancelor "The Fox" Ivarel
    (role) Retired Agent
    (book) Volume V: The Black Ragnarok
    (description) A former Black Ragnarok agent known as "The Fox" who retired to raise a family. He lost his left eye in the line of duty and was reluctant to return to the shadows. He stayed behind to hold a corridor in St. Jude's so the others could walk out; no body was ever recovered.
    (status) Unknown (Held the Corridor)

  > (character)
    (name) Palwin Condervale
    (role) Active Agent / Strategist
    (book) Volume V: The Black Ragnarok
    (description) A sharp, seasoned operative of Black Ragnarok who never left the agency. She fed what remained of it just enough to keep it patient, and it was she who sent the letter that woke Soren—Freya's phrase, in Freya's hand. She was never the traitor. She was the delay.
    (status) Active (Loyalty Proven)

  > (character)
    (name) Muatti
    (role) Scientist / Defector
    (book) Volume VII: The Elegy
    (description) A money-driven researcher who clawed his way out of the alleys into a white coat at St. Jude's. Promoted to study the Touch of Rose patients after his superior went mad, he became the first to measure the eleven-hour pulse from the inside—and to grasp its horror: the Rose-Marked are not broadcasting but answering a call beneath the mountain. He tried to destroy Project Glacier's data and was marked for death.
    (status) Critically Wounded

  > (character)
    (name) Doctor Crale
    (role) Chief Researcher
    (book) Volume VII: The Elegy
    (description) Muatti's brilliant, untouchable predecessor at St. Jude's. Prolonged exposure to the RedLink's Proxanian Echo shattered his mind; he was committed raving of twelve hearts beating as one drum and a black sun beneath the mountain. His breakdown opened the post that Muatti was promoted to fill.
    (status) Insane (Institutionalized)

  > (character)
    (name) Pugion
    (role) Prizefighter / Enforcer
    (book) Volume VII: The Elegy
    (description) An unbeatable fighter in the arenas of Glareach. After the men he had crossed murdered his wife and daughter in a staged "traffic accident," grief hollowed him out and they made him their weapon—pointing him at marked men in the ring and laundering the kills as sport. The crowd knows only the name "Pugion"; the husband and father who once owned the older name is gone.
    (status) Unknown (Walked into the Dark)

  > (character)
    (name) The Smiling Man
    (role) Handler / Fixer
    (book) Volume VII: The Elegy
    (description) A towel-draped cornerman whose grin never reaches his eyes. Pugion first saw his face leaning over a hospital bed after the "accident" that took his family, and has felt the same cold dread every time since. He delivers Pugion to the ring, and to the suited men who own him.
    (status) Active